{
  "id": "29985_hasshin",
  "headword": "{発進|はっしん}",
  "reading": "はっしん",
  "romaji": "hasshin",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "starting off; moving off; departure",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "starting off; moving off (of a vehicle)",
      "explanation": "The act of a stationary vehicle, ship, or aircraft beginning to move. Composed of {発|はつ} (to set out) and {進|しん} (to advance). Takes する; used chiefly of vehicles, not people."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29985_hasshin_ex1",
      "japanese": "{車|くるま}が{発進|はっしん}した。",
      "english": "The car pulled away.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29985_hasshin_ex2",
      "japanese": "{信号|しんごう}が{青|あお}になって{発進|はっしん}する。",
      "english": "The light turns green and I move off.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29985_hasshin_ex3",
      "japanese": "アクセルを{踏|ふ}みすぎると{急発進|きゅうはっしん}して{危|あぶ}ない。",
      "english": "Pressing the accelerator too hard causes a sudden start, which is dangerous.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The counterpart to {停止|ていし} (stopping); refers to a vehicle beginning to move, not a person setting out.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {発進|はっしん}する: to move off; to pull away\n- {急発進|きゅうはっしん}: sudden start\n- スムーズに{発進|はっしん}する: to move off smoothly\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {出発|しゅっぱつ}: departure — the broader word for setting out on a journey, used of people and scheduled services\n- {発車|はっしゃ}: (a train or bus) departing from a stop",
